WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.203
-My first guest tonight is
a very funny comedian

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:04.737
who you know from
"Saturday Night Live."

00:00:04.737 --> 00:00:07.573
He and Jon Stewart
are putting on a show called

00:00:07.573 --> 00:00:11.711
"NYC Still Rising After
20 Years: A Comedy Celebration"

00:00:11.711 --> 00:00:13.946
this Sunday
at Madison Square Garden.

00:00:13.946 --> 00:00:15.247
Tickets are available now.

00:00:15.247 --> 00:00:17.550
Everyone, please welcome
Pete Davidson!

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.551
[ Cheers and applause ]
♪♪

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:21.053
-♪ Pete Davidson ♪

00:00:21.053 --> 00:00:23.556
♪ Ain't no mystery ♪

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.061
♪ Pete Davidson ♪

00:00:29.061 --> 00:00:31.564
♪ Simply can't compare ♪

00:00:31.564 --> 00:00:33.766
♪ Yeah ♪
-They love you.

00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:36.335
-Very cool.
-That's some love.

00:00:36.335 --> 00:00:38.504
That's some love for
Pete Davidson right there.

00:00:38.504 --> 00:00:40.039
-It's a full crowd.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:40.039 --> 00:00:42.241
-Right.
-Oh, wow.

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:44.910
-Thank you for being here.
I appreciate you coming back.

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.679
-Thanks for having me.

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:48.281
-"SNL" had a great season
last year.

00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:49.448
You had had
a great season, as well,

00:00:49.448 --> 00:00:51.150
so congrats again on that.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:53.619
I wanted to ask you a question,
though, because there was

00:00:53.619 --> 00:00:54.620
an episode where I know --

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:55.621
I knew you were
friends with him.

00:00:55.621 --> 00:00:59.425
But it was
Machine Gun Kelly and you

00:00:59.425 --> 00:01:00.993
are at the end of the show,
at goodnights,

00:01:00.993 --> 00:01:03.195
and you're kind of
hugging and celebrating.

00:01:03.195 --> 00:01:04.931
And then
you fall off the stage.

00:01:04.931 --> 00:01:06.465
-Yeah.

00:01:06.465 --> 00:01:07.967
-What was going --
What's the real story?

00:01:07.967 --> 00:01:09.368
What happened?

00:01:09.368 --> 00:01:13.807
-So, Colson -- or as you may
know him as Machine Gun Kelly --

00:01:13.807 --> 00:01:19.578
he bruised his coccyx that week.

00:01:19.578 --> 00:01:23.449
If you don't know what a coccyx
is, it's the bone in your ass.

00:01:23.449 --> 00:01:24.650
-Okay. Oh, okay. Yeah.

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:26.185
-Yeah, it's from --
If you've ever seen

00:01:26.185 --> 00:01:28.822
"Napoleon Dynamite,"
Uncle Rico says,

00:01:28.822 --> 00:01:30.189
"Grandma took
a spill at the dunes.

00:01:30.189 --> 00:01:31.523
She broke her coccyx."
Yeah.

00:01:31.523 --> 00:01:34.160
-That's a good reference.
-So, I thought he was joking.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.528
He was like,
"I broke my coccyx."

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:37.029
-He broke his coccyx?
-Or he bruised it.

00:01:37.029 --> 00:01:38.531
And I was like, "Oh, that's..."

00:01:38.531 --> 00:01:39.531
He was like, "No, for real."

00:01:39.531 --> 00:01:41.100
So he couldn't,
like, walk or sit

00:01:41.100 --> 00:01:43.703
and he had, like,
a tushy pillow that he was --

00:01:43.703 --> 00:01:44.903
It was just really cool
to see, like,

00:01:44.903 --> 00:01:47.540
the most
gangster, thug dude I know

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:49.342
just, like, put a little tushy
pillow down and, like, sit.

00:01:49.342 --> 00:01:50.576
-Inflatable ring.

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:52.511
-Yeah, it's just, like,
Megan Fox is right there,

00:01:52.511 --> 00:01:55.848
and he's sitting on
his little tushy pillow.

00:01:55.848 --> 00:01:57.783
So, he was like,
"For goodnights,

00:01:57.783 --> 00:01:59.552
we should do something,
you know, silly."

00:01:59.552 --> 00:02:00.720
And I was like, "Or, you know,

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:02.355
you could just
enjoy the moment and clap."

00:02:02.355 --> 00:02:03.556
-Yeah.

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:05.791
-And he was like,
"No, we'll think of something.

00:02:05.791 --> 00:02:07.627
I'm going to,
like, pick you up."

00:02:07.627 --> 00:02:09.195
I was like, "I don't know
if you should do that.

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:11.130
It's a crowded stage.
You know, we should just clap."

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:13.132
And he's like, "Yeah, yeah,
you're right."

00:02:13.132 --> 00:02:16.636
And he got really excited
and he went to pick me up

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:19.605
and he forgot that he had
a bruised coccyx.

00:02:19.605 --> 00:02:23.843
So he, like, went to pick me up,
and then he couldn't go up,

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:25.778
so he just started to
slowly tilt back.

00:02:25.778 --> 00:02:27.513
And he went --
he went, "Oh, no."

00:02:27.513 --> 00:02:30.283
And it was such a slow fall,
we had time for him to go,

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:33.886
"Oh, no," and I went,
"You're a [bleep] moron."

00:02:33.886 --> 00:02:35.722
And --
-It was that slow of a fall.

00:02:35.722 --> 00:02:36.889
-It was that slow.

00:02:36.889 --> 00:02:39.993
I got the full line out.
-Also, you're a big dude.

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:41.827
-We're both pretty tall dudes.
-Yes.

00:02:41.827 --> 00:02:44.764
-And we have no, like --
It's hard to pick me up,

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:46.766
'cause I'm so, like,
flimsy and bony.

00:02:46.766 --> 00:02:49.068
So, like, yeah, it was --
-I have a clip.

00:02:49.068 --> 00:02:50.336
-Oh, great.
-I want to show everyone.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:54.540
Here's Machine Gun Kelly
trying to pick Pete up on "SNL."

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:55.641
Take a look at this.
-Yep.

00:02:55.641 --> 00:02:57.677
♪♪

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:03.750
-Dude, I was like, "Yo!"
-Yeah.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:04.817
-That was --

00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:06.785
-And then they
cut right after that.

00:03:06.785 --> 00:03:09.122
They went right to --
they went right to

00:03:09.122 --> 00:03:10.456
whatever the next thing was.

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:13.092
So, I went to -- Nobody ever
texts me during a show.

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:14.661
I went back,
there was like 40 texts like,

00:03:14.661 --> 00:03:16.595
"Yo, you alive?"

00:03:16.595 --> 00:03:18.064
Yeah.
-That was so funny, dude.

00:03:18.064 --> 00:03:19.365
-Yeah.

00:03:19.365 --> 00:03:21.667
-Last time you were on the show,
we were talking about

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:23.502
"Suicide Squad" and "SNL,"

00:03:23.502 --> 00:03:26.405
and I think I remember you
telling me that you got a dog.

00:03:26.405 --> 00:03:27.406
And I was like,
"That's awesome."

00:03:27.406 --> 00:03:29.374
-Yeah.
-Congrats on that.

00:03:29.374 --> 00:03:30.643
-Thank you.
-Yeah. And then --

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:33.079
[ Cheers and applause ]
-It's a big deal. Yeah.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:34.680
-And now you came back here

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:36.549
and you just told me,
backstage --

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:38.217
You go, "Hey, dude,
everything's cool.

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:39.352
I just got a dog."

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:40.886
And I go, "Yeah,
you told me that already."

00:03:40.886 --> 00:03:45.624
-Yeah, I got three dogs during
the pandemic, 'cause it's hard.

00:03:45.624 --> 00:03:50.630
No, I got the first dog,
like, for me,

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:52.898
but I had to leave
and go do something,

00:03:52.898 --> 00:03:54.634
so it had to stay with my mom.

00:03:54.634 --> 00:03:56.135
And then, when I came back,

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:59.571
the dog was, like,
really tight with my mom.

00:03:59.571 --> 00:04:01.941
Like, more --
Like, it wasn't as excited

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:04.043
to see me as it was my mom.

00:04:04.043 --> 00:04:06.145
So I bought another one.

00:04:06.145 --> 00:04:08.147
-Yeah.

00:04:08.147 --> 00:04:10.984
-And then,
same situation happened,

00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:12.451
where I had to go away
for a little bit,

00:04:12.451 --> 00:04:14.620
but I was like, "Can't leave it
with my mom, 'cause she --"

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:15.888
-No. You saw what happened.

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:17.589
-Yeah, I saw what
happened to the first one.

00:04:17.589 --> 00:04:18.658
So I gave it to my sister,

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:21.360
'cause she's less lovable
of the Davidsons.

00:04:21.360 --> 00:04:24.063
No, I'm just kidding.
She's wonderful.

00:04:24.063 --> 00:04:27.066
She actually just got her coat.
She got coated.

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:28.768
She's, like,
a registered nurse now.

00:04:28.768 --> 00:04:29.868
-Hey! There you go.
-Yeah.

00:04:29.868 --> 00:04:31.103
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:04:31.103 --> 00:04:35.508
So, I was like, "Safe.
I'll give her the dog."

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:37.809
And then I came back.
Same thing happened.

00:04:37.809 --> 00:04:41.046
The dog was really in love
with my sister and not me.

00:04:41.046 --> 00:04:46.085
So I bought a third dog, and now
she's with me all the time.

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:47.619
-Now, what kind of dog
is this dog?

00:04:47.619 --> 00:04:49.021
-I'm allergic to all dogs,

00:04:49.021 --> 00:04:50.856
so they all have to be a poodle
or, like, a poodle mix.

00:04:50.856 --> 00:04:51.924
-Right.

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:52.992
-So they're all
poodles and, like --

00:04:52.992 --> 00:04:54.193
-Poodle-doodles?
-Yeah.

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:55.194
They're really --
They're like this big.

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:56.595
They so cute.

00:04:56.595 --> 00:04:58.597
And this one -- This one, I
think, is going to stay with me.

00:04:58.597 --> 00:04:59.865
Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:59.865 --> 00:05:01.566
-Now you've got three dogs.
-Yeah.

00:05:01.566 --> 00:05:02.668
-What are their names?

00:05:02.668 --> 00:05:05.070
-Mabel, Henry, and Lock.
-Yeah.

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:06.105
-Yeah.
-Those are great names.

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:07.106
-Yeah, yeah.

00:05:07.106 --> 00:05:08.240
-I like straight-up names
for a dog.

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:10.843
-I like straight-up,
regular names, like Joe.

00:05:10.843 --> 00:05:13.579
-Yeah. Yeah.
Yeah, my dog is Gary.

00:05:13.579 --> 00:05:15.514
-Yeah. It's so funny.
-I love it. Yeah. Why not?

00:05:15.514 --> 00:05:17.116
-"What's up, Gary?"
-Yeah, Gary.

00:05:17.116 --> 00:05:18.450
It's like,
"Gary, get over here."

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:20.886
It's, like, some cute
golden retriever coming over.

00:05:20.886 --> 00:05:22.621
I want to ask you quickly.

00:05:22.621 --> 00:05:24.923
I know you're getting ready
to work on a couple of projects,

00:05:24.923 --> 00:05:27.994
but one project you're working
on I'm very excited about.

00:05:27.994 --> 00:05:29.595
You're going to play
Joey Ramone?

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:31.463
-Yes. That is --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:31.463 --> 00:05:32.999
Yeah. Thank you. Yeah.

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:37.002
I would also be
hesitant to clap, as well.

00:05:37.002 --> 00:05:39.138
-No.
-No, it's the craziest thing.

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:41.841
It was like a year or two ago,
I got a call.

00:05:41.841 --> 00:05:43.743
They were like, "Would you like
to play Joey Ramone?"

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:45.578
And I was like, "Yeah."
-Of course.

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:47.513
-But I thought
it wasn't, like, a real thing.

00:05:47.513 --> 00:05:50.049
And then it became a real thing.

00:05:50.049 --> 00:05:52.218
So now, yeah, hopefully
in January or February,

00:05:52.218 --> 00:05:53.218
we'll start.

00:05:53.218 --> 00:05:54.587
-This is amazing, buddy.

00:05:54.587 --> 00:05:56.088
I never heard you sing.

00:05:56.088 --> 00:05:58.724
-I can't.
-There you go. This is perfect.

00:05:58.724 --> 00:06:00.659
-As a joke -- This is true.

00:06:00.659 --> 00:06:02.361
Three years ago,
I started taking

00:06:02.361 --> 00:06:04.597
singing lessons as a joke,
because I --

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:07.266
No, I just thought it would be
funny if, like, one day, like,

00:06:07.266 --> 00:06:09.301
I was just hanging out
with the boys

00:06:09.301 --> 00:06:12.371
and, like --
And just belted out a song.

00:06:12.371 --> 00:06:13.472
-I know what
you're talking about.

00:06:13.472 --> 00:06:14.873
-Yeah, you know?
-That would be a good bit.

00:06:14.873 --> 00:06:16.576
-Just kicking it
with the boys in the most

00:06:16.576 --> 00:06:19.978
un-song-friendly environment
and then just belt out, like,

00:06:19.978 --> 00:06:21.147
Sinatra or something.

00:06:21.147 --> 00:06:22.881
Yeah, so,
I've been going to this --

00:06:22.881 --> 00:06:25.918
For like a year,
I went to this guy who --

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:28.287
He's a voice coach of the stars.

00:06:28.287 --> 00:06:29.455
-Wow!

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:32.124
-And I remember
going up to his apartment,

00:06:32.124 --> 00:06:33.792
and he was like,
"This is so great.

00:06:33.792 --> 00:06:35.294
This is cool
we get to work together."

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:37.229
He's like,
"What project is this for?"

00:06:37.229 --> 00:06:40.332
And I was like,
"This is for my pure enjoyment."

00:06:40.332 --> 00:06:42.535
-Nothing. I'm just here to hang
and learn something.

00:06:42.535 --> 00:06:43.736
-I can't sing yet,

00:06:43.736 --> 00:06:45.104
but I know what
it's supposed to sound like.

00:06:45.104 --> 00:06:46.505
-Alright, good.
-Yeah.

00:06:46.505 --> 00:06:47.673
-I can't wait for that.
I think it's going to be great.

00:06:47.673 --> 00:06:49.074
-Oh, one day,
I will belt it out.

00:06:49.074 --> 00:06:50.109
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:06:50.109 --> 00:06:51.109
-I want to talk about
this Sunday.

00:06:51.109 --> 00:06:52.878
Madison Square Garden,

00:06:52.878 --> 00:06:57.149
"NYC Still Rising After
20 Years: A Comedy Celebration."

00:06:57.149 --> 00:06:58.450
Listen to all these comedians

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:01.120
that are going to be
at the Garden this Sunday.

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:02.989
Amy Schumer, Bill Burr,

00:07:02.989 --> 00:07:06.859
Colin Jost, Colin Quinn,
Dave Attell, Dave Chappelle,

00:07:06.859 --> 00:07:12.531
John Mulaney, Jon Stewart,
Michael Che.

00:07:12.531 --> 00:07:14.633
[ Cheers and applause ]
I'm going to be there.

00:07:14.633 --> 00:07:15.902
-Jimmy's going to be there.
-I'm gonna be -- Yeah.

00:07:15.902 --> 00:07:17.203
-Yep.
Thank you. I appreciate that.

00:07:17.203 --> 00:07:18.237
-Very nice of you to --

00:07:18.237 --> 00:07:19.738
You know,
I know you're a busy guy,

00:07:19.738 --> 00:07:20.739
so thanks for doing that.

00:07:20.739 --> 00:07:22.175
-Are you kidding me?

00:07:22.175 --> 00:07:24.243
You sent me a text and you go,
"Well, I might put this thing on

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:25.744
with Jon,
and would you be interested?"

00:07:25.744 --> 00:07:26.979
And I go, "Anything."

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:29.181
Obviously, for the
city and for you, I'd do it.

00:07:29.181 --> 00:07:31.450
But, I mean,
was it hard to get all these --

00:07:31.450 --> 00:07:33.853
This is --
-The lineup is nuts.

00:07:33.853 --> 00:07:38.557
Yeah, it's like
the Avengers and me.

00:07:38.557 --> 00:07:40.559
No, it was --
It was really cool.

00:07:40.559 --> 00:07:42.194
Me and Jon
just reached out to --

00:07:42.194 --> 00:07:43.962
Luckily,
we have really great friends,

00:07:43.962 --> 00:07:45.531
and we reached out,

00:07:45.531 --> 00:07:47.532
and everybody was
super-stoked to do it.

00:07:47.532 --> 00:07:49.668
And it was just like --
You know,

00:07:49.668 --> 00:07:51.937
it's obviously, like,
a thing that's, like,

00:07:51.937 --> 00:07:53.472
close to me and stuff,
so I got --

00:07:53.472 --> 00:07:55.741
A lot of people
wanted to do, like, a thing,

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:57.376
like some sort of, like --

00:07:57.376 --> 00:07:59.077
you know, like,
an article or, like --

00:07:59.077 --> 00:08:00.279
And it all
just felt really weird.

00:08:00.279 --> 00:08:02.181
So I just called Jon
and I was like,

00:08:02.181 --> 00:08:04.683
"We should do something fun,
like a fun little party,

00:08:04.683 --> 00:08:06.018
and, like,
just have a good time."

00:08:06.018 --> 00:08:07.553
So that's how it came together.

00:08:07.553 --> 00:08:09.154
And he does a lot, you know,

00:08:09.154 --> 00:08:11.290
